Introduction / Background

(Owner: Precious & David)

This project examines the patterns and predictors of fatal vehicle crashes across the United States using data from the Fatality Analysis Reporting System (FARS). We investigate how crash outcomes vary based on geographic, temporal, vehicle, and driver characteristics.

In our progress report, we identified three research questions motivated by prior literature on rural vs. urban crash severity, weekend/weekday crash patterns, and night-time risk factors. Below, we restate these questions along with the formal analyses we conducted to answer them.

